got featured in LWN.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.230
And you can see there's a lot
of deep understanding of what's

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.960
really going on in this
new space with containers

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.930
and security.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:57.332
What's nice is that with
Anthos, when these things are

00:04:57.332 --> 00:04:58.790
happening, it's
really hard to keep

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:00.890
track of microservice
security and what's

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:03.770
going on in that barrier
between containers in the OS.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.420
We have an integrated
solution that we

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.160
take care of that for the user.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.410
Keeping track of your operating
system, your container

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:12.110
technology, your Kubernetes,
and what happened in the latest

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:12.740
release--

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:13.627
it's hard.

00:05:13.627 --> 00:05:14.960
It's very hard to keep on track.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.080
And we have that expertise.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.480
You don't have to
worry about it.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.590
The other part is kind of
a more boring part, which

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:23.850
is keeping things up to date.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:25.850
It's not easy to do
with open source.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:28.310
And staying on top
of the latest CDEs,

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.190
knowing which ones
are worthy of upgrade

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.940
and which ones aren't,
it's something else

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.260
that Anthos is about.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.960
So we've started and designed
it from the beginning

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:39.260
to think about upgradability and
doing that all the way, again,

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:42.410
down to the stack, with the
operating system, the host OS,

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:45.323
the container OSes, and all
the parts of Kubernetes.

00:05:45.323 --> 00:05:47.240
That's the part that's
much more of the grind.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:49.100
But it's the piece
that you really

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:52.603
want to outsource
because you just do.

00:05:52.603 --> 00:05:53.270
