00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.960
They're using Istio.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:58.460
And in the last six months have
migrated about 186 services

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:03.620
from an on-prem VM based cluster
to a GKE cluster using Istio.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:06.078
And what's beautiful
is that they

00:07:06.078 --> 00:07:08.120
didn't change their
developer experiences at all.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:10.220
They have a very
good CI/CD pipeline.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:13.610
And they changed the output
of that CI/CD pipeline, which

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.910
used to compile a
jar, spin up a VM,

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.980
and then deploy
that jar to the VM.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:22.760
Now instead, their developers
still use the same CI/CD,

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:24.300
but they've modified
their pipeline

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.160
so it produces a container
and it deploys that container

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.900
into GKE.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.052
And the beauty of what they
did was that they already--

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:35.510
they were disciplined enough
to already not have developers

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:38.030
who are off, you know,
SSH-ing into hosts

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.410
to get things involved.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:40.910
They had done some automation.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:45.410
And when they adopted, kind of
changed the platform completely

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:48.530
underneath, it didn't
affect their developers.

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.880
And that's been a big deal.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:52.730
They are now multilingual,
where they could only

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:53.982
handle jars before.

00:07:53.982 --> 00:07:55.940
Now the developers use
the appropriate language

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.530
for the appropriate tool.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.970
They have better insight than
ever into their application

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:01.120
and how it's running.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.290
But what would enable that whole
thing was a good, robust CI/CD

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.960
